IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s393-s398-miscellaneous`

-- Tests of dg11-s393-s398-miscellaneous.l4 (sections 393, 394, 396, 397, 398).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section, beside the assertion.

§ `Section 393 - rights, liabilities and duties under prior statutes`

-- src:2084: the four named kinds, arising "by and under" an earlier law, are unimpaired by this chapter.
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a right, privilege or immunity vested or accrued under an earlier law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a suit pending under an earlier law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a right of action conferred by an earlier law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a duty, restriction, liability or penalty imposed or required by an earlier law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A right that did not arise under an earlier law, and a thing of a kind the text does not name: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a right, privilege or immunity vested or accrued under an earlier law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a thing of another kind that s 393 does not name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `a thing of another kind that s 393 does not name` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 394 - reserved power of the State; the chapter as part of the charter`

-- src:2088, first sentence: a remedy under this chapter against a corporation or its officers, for a liability previously incurred, survives.
#ASSERT `s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A remedy not under this chapter, or a liability not yet incurred when the chapter is amended: the sentence does not speak to them.
#ASSERT `s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:2088, second sentence: part of the charter "except so far as" inapplicable AND inappropriate; both are needed to be excepted.
#ASSERT NOT `s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 396 - publication of the chapter by the Secretary of State`

-- src:2102, first clause: the Secretary of State may have copies printed when the Secretary of State deems it necessary
#ASSERT `s 396 the Secretary of State may have pamphlet copies of this chapter printed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 396 the Secretary of State may have pamphlet copies of this chapter printed` FALSE
-- src:2102, second sentence: the money from the sale is treated as other fees of the office; money from elsewhere is not addressed
#ASSERT `s 396 the money received from the sale of the copies is disposed of as other fees of the office of the Secretary of State` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396 the money received from the sale of the copies is disposed of as other fees of the office of the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2102: "a sum not exceeding the cost of printing": equal to the cost is inside the limit, a cent above it is outside.
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` 5 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` 4.99 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` 5.01 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` 0 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A negative sum or a negative cost is not a case the section describes.
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` (0 MINUS 1) 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` 5 (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:2102, last sentence: "single pamphlet copies" may be distributed free; more than one, or none, is not addressed.
#ASSERT `s 396 this section does not prevent the free distribution` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396 this section does not prevent the free distribution` 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 396 this section does not prevent the free distribution` 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 397 - penalty for unauthorized publication of the chapter`

-- src:2106: "not more than $500 or ... not more than 3 months, or both".
#ASSERT `s 397 the greatest fine for printing or publishing this chapter without authority` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 397 the greatest term of imprisonment, in months, for printing or publishing this chapter without authority` EQUALS 3
-- The offence: prints or publishes, without the authority of the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `s 397 the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 397 the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 397 the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` FALSE FALSE
-- The penalty limits, both edges: $500 and 3 months are inside; $500.01 and 3 months and a day (3.1 months) are outside.
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE 500 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE 500.01 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE 500 3.1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE 500 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` TRUE (0 MINUS 1) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A person who has not printed or published without authority: the text gives no penalty, so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` FALSE 100 1 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 398 - short title`

-- src:2110
#ASSERT `s 398 the short title of the chapter` EQUALS "General Corporation Law of the State of Delaware"
#ASSERT `s 398 the name may be used to refer to the chapter` "General Corporation Law of the State of Delaware" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another name: "may be identified and referred to as" does not forbid it, but does not license it either.
#ASSERT `s 398 the name may be used to refer to the chapter` "the Delaware corporation statute" EQUALS NOTHING
